{"title":"2010 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2(Trig_and_Angle_Chasing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2(Trig and Angle Chasing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Similar_Triangles)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Similar Triangles)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_the_Beauty_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by the Beauty of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8459f4fd4283e7a890e90d0d1e8a12165e67c25f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=2 \\cdot AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, respectively, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbdeefcd1a978cd2665988a36c42ef35d6d315ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAE = \\angle ACD$\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/803aa1ba74919a869eee5f679bb42af62b79d343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CFE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/0728bebb477a2636300c56851b6a6f9e382c1b83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebfe6916978622edf7ebab8e74de4a65129ef6ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 60^\\circ \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 75^\\circ \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 90^\\circ \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 105^\\circ \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"449\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_2010_12A_Problem_8.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/9/90/AMC_2010_12A_Problem_8.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"648\" height=\"486\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></center>\n<p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4b979c0312ea3b49caae04567ad62d409009a90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAE = \\angle ACD = x$\" width=\"170\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9c17f4dce1274d718fa93f9b33b771dc24d9d28.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\angle BCD &amp;= \\angle AEC = 60^\\circ\\\\  \\angle EAC + \\angle FCA + \\angle ECF + \\angle AEC &amp;= \\angle EAC + x + 60^\\circ + 60^\\circ = 180^\\circ\\\\  \\angle EAC &amp;= 60^\\circ - x\\\\  \\angle BAC &amp;= \\angle EAC + \\angle BAE = 60^\\circ - x + x = 60^\\circ\\end{align*}\" width=\"608\" height=\"89\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf3fbd1db608066d455da37f0192f9b22b5f9dc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AC}{AB} = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" /> and the angle between the hypotenuse and the shorter side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e997fe9c2a91f20b4948c1215002963cca79fa29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCA = \\boxed{90^\\circ\\,\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"149\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2.28Trig_and_Angle_Chasing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2(Trig_and_Angle_Chasing)\">Solution 2(Trig and Angle Chasing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2(Trig and Angle Chasing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6e31a542a4951d6c36ddec800070839dca8ae43.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB=2a, AC=a\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf58fffe97b3734e02c30ef3f365306a585164e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BAE=\\angle ACD=x\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"13\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/803aa1ba74919a869eee5f679bb42af62b79d343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CFE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ce283ce0b07e6c6c748c8c819b58c82ffdac3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FCE=60$\" width=\"97\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0db72d6106a470ab52ce76939695185115c6356.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB=60+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"130\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/803aa1ba74919a869eee5f679bb42af62b79d343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CFE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is equilateral, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d586ace5604c976307d350099c8f18bc9f53764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CFE=60$\" width=\"97\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/d/45d262ec0040725407c96f2c9e81ff7919b0192b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFD$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/b/90b9a295c4e5f02afdc79a10c5493c3acbbc4a81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CFE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> are vertical, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df6baeb7348f1607c9b4d13ce707ee93204239c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AFD=60$\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>By triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651bffb059906f373d826a5030b415fdc31e3729.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/899c0e1bfb1b2968b48a892438671bc4c7f03497.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADF=120-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"140\" height=\"13\" />, and because of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c365538e8cdb88bbf1e3210f94498132aadf144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDC=60+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Because Of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/4/c3411b59e7d1d47481ba91f800b7f60e3971001c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AEB=120$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" />, and by line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d65190471539b1bc16030cda329310db9a0e8810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DFE=120$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"108\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>By quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/1/38142ecb9f1316fd00881a995d30f9f30c88bbf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDFE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9adf5c91b80ea174234a9358433726f291775429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC=60-x$\" width=\"130\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>By the Law of Sines:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/e/d7e6b9a16af214b8acfe3ba1b8b6f52ca5ea9a79.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin(60-x)}{a}=\\frac{\\sin(60+x)}{2a}\\implies 2\\sin(60-x)=\\sin(60+x)\\]\" width=\"463\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>By the sine addition formula(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/7/327a43563ed80eabce335bbe6b048cf242edb055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(a+b)=\\sin(a)\\cos(b)+\\cos(a)\\sin(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"312\" height=\"18\" />):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd837236a65877160af4925f89cc035ee006bea7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(\\sin(60)\\cos(-x)+\\cos(60)\\sin(-x))=\\sin(60)\\cos(x)+\\cos(60)\\sin(x)\\]\" width=\"528\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Because cosine is an even function, and sine is an odd function, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b3d3d54ea9c15ce92878223b9a229e5732693ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\sin(60)\\cos(x)-2\\cos(60)\\sin(x)=\\sin(60)\\cos(x)+\\cos(60)\\sin(x) \\implies \\sin(60)\\cos(x)=3\\cos(60)\\sin(x)\\]\" width=\"800\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/9/739e0ab88a48f1d549cb6d5a10f75268fb86bb3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(60)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"105\" height=\"41\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdcc2e3f1e8c6ef5c3de7c824ccacb1470ccb39e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(60)=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"92\" height=\"37\" />, hence \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b1feb7eb723f560404b76942ee2b9e60f7b0cb0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cos(x)=\\frac{3}{2}\\sin(x)\\implies \\tan(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\]\" width=\"316\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>The only value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e189c35231de4880ef342366a1de267896031f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60+x&lt;180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"14\" />(because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/181492c1df8351d884cb355affe69d166019b02b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> is an angle of the triangle) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf0e92c388dfabeadb2eb39f51dda5d5e94c050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=30^{\\circ}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />. We seek to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/0728bebb477a2636300c56851b6a6f9e382c1b83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, which as we found before is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/181492c1df8351d884cb355affe69d166019b02b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8acca8e3a9a437596efcc51568f72b39b4226a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90, \\text{or} \\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>-vsamc\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Similar_Triangles.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Similar_Triangles)\">Solution 3 (Similar Triangles)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Similar Triangles)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e57f722f42d6ed542a474948896b9edd210d782f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AEB=\\angle AFC = 120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"192\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1eb4d32f738a10240a75bd9dbf74cf765888c4b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACF=\\angle BAE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"137\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, triangle AEB is similar to triangle CFA. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/6/636ec0206fba13f9e8c19261fc6c8156633079b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=2AC$\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7f9b1bc5ece1822e221a2313be5a7eccfdfeece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=2CF=2FE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"154\" height=\"14\" />, as triangle CFE is equilateral. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/6/ff6949022a4b0917991711f89c62c1fdf2e2c991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF=FE=FC$\" width=\"133\" height=\"13\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/4/304991b80634de00d06e015943ba23667f4ae254.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AFC=120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"112\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f3f18e15c1e5cb4ab85abcb01eac951b30875b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=30$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />. Thus, the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/291b6d0f956fd6c89571701ea806380d94e34e55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> equals to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/5803efb99997926cbc5309d5266f59a3eecef1c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FCE+\\angle ACF=90^{\\circ}, \\text{or} \\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"233\" height=\"17\" /> \n-HarryW\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24b4240c4af16727d4a6542f475cb53900203597.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADF \\sim \\triangle CDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" /> (by AA Similarity.) Since the corresponding angles of a pair of similar triangles are congruent, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73d3275566fc0c0904872dd050d243d16603278c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAC = \\angle DFA = 60^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"194\" height=\"15\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be269899357294cce2e8ac4ebaaa98462ffa1eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 2 \\cdot AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a402c8c141f6612ffc90d9c6a532db50638b3939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DFA = 60^\\circ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" /> we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is congruent by SAS to a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> right triangle, which gives the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n~clever14710owl\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_the_Beauty_of_Math\">Video Solution by the Beauty of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by the Beauty of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/kU70k1-ONgM?t=785\">https://youtu.be/kU70k1-ONgM?t=785</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/O_o_-yjGrOU?t=58\">https://youtu.be/O_o_-yjGrOU?t=58</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A\">2010 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2010 AMC